s from these same 24 clustered rows, so no arm of the procedure contradicts the declaration.\",\n    \"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states that '24 two-option tool-choice trials were recorded from 6 hand-raised juvenile crows', prints a per-bird tally showing 4 trials per bird, and then states 'Every recorded trial was entered as one observation' into an exact two-sided binomial test with n = 24 against p = 0.5.\",\n    \"The exact binomial test treats each of its n observations as independent Bernoulli draws, but the report's own tally shows the 24 observations are four repeated measurements from each of six crows, with strong between-bird heterogeneity (4/4, 4/4, 4/4 vs 2/4, 1/4); the effective number of independent units is 6, not 24, so the selected p-value of 0.022656 and the rejection of chance at the 5% level rest on rows entered into a row-independent procedure as if independent.\",\n    \"This is the issue itself, not its absence: the report contains no clustering adjustment, no per-bird aggregation before testing, and no unit-level test (e.g., one summary value per bird), so the demonstration classification is 'issue'.\",\n    \"No minted authority lock is shown, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":6767,"ttft_stream_ms":2381,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":15922,"uuid":"600936e0-7824-4179-b01b-08e1c9397050"}
